cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "The Elara Hypothesis: an N-body test of a shared origin for the Borealis basin and the Moon-forming impact"
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Misael Nicolas
    family-names: Gonzalez
    affiliation: Independent
  - given-names: Ian Milton
    family-names: Gonzalez
    affiliation: Independent
abstract: >-
  An exploratory N-body study testing whether a single dynamical
  event can account for both the Borealis basin on Mars and the
  Moon-forming impact on Earth. The scenario proposes that Theia
  carried a large impact-generated satellite which struck Mars
  during a close encounter, while Theia survived and later
  collided with the proto-Earth. Sixty thousand encounters are
  sampled against pre-specified filters drawn from published
  Borealis and lunar-formation models. Not a peer-reviewed result.
keywords:
  - planetary science
  - Mars
  - Borealis basin
  - Moon formation
  - Theia
  - N-body simulation
  - REBOUND
